^warning: ignoring
--
id() now returns a deterministic identity (address of the object's
storage cast to int) for addressable operands, so id(x) == id(x)
holds, an alias y = x shares x's id, and a distinct list has a
distinct id. Previously id() fell through to a nondet int.
